  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows high volatility or a downward trend followed by a spike; true outcomes often reverse immediately after the forecast's initial rise.",
    "When sentiment is near zero (0.00) but price history shows a sharp drop, the model fails to capture the subsequent recovery spike seen in true outcomes.",
    "The model consistently overestimates the magnitude of short-term rallies and underestimates the depth of immediate corrections following volatility events.",
    "Forecasts assume smooth linear growth based on recent highs, ignoring the mean-reverting nature of EU ETS prices during high-volatility periods.",
    "When sentiment history contains isolated positive spikes (0.20) amidst neutral noise, the model ignores these signals and continues a trend that contradicts actual price action."
  ]
}
